{"id":"[REDACTED]","object":"chat.completion","created":1790942023,"model":"mercury-2","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"record_type\": \"reduction\",\n  \"summary\": \"The review examined all 11 source files in the repository (mercury.config.json, adversarial-review.js, ask.js, codex-challenger.js, config.js, consensus.js, doctrine-review.js, llm-client.js, provider-preflight.js, reviewer-panel.js, run-ledger.js). No defects were found in the majority of files; however, three substantive issues were identified: (1) flagFromEnv silently returns false for any non‑empty, unrecognized environment value (adversarial-review.js:122‑129); (2) optionalEnvBoolean silently defaults to false for unknown env strings (config.js:81‑87); (3) removal of the Opus fallback in provider‑preflight reduces provider coverage (provider-preflight.js:232‑246, llm-client.js:118‑124). The fourth‑shape classifier recorded eight added throw statements across several modules. Inherited‑pattern inspection detected the presence of the patterns “|| 0”, “swallowed catch”, “bypass env”, and “silent default”. Several mapper shards were malformed, leaving unresolved unit IDs and missing records. Numerous AST fragments were incomplete, yielding unresolved findings. Overall candidate inventory was fully examined (11 of 11).\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"claim-4280d853568adc54e9463f91\",\n      \"type\": \"MECHANICAL\",\n      \"basis\": \"RECEIPT\",\n      \"description\": \"flagFromEnv returns false for any non‑empty, non‑recognized env value, providing no diagnostic output.\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        \"trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:122-129\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"config-optionalEnvBoolean\",\n      \"type\": \"MECHANICAL\",\n      \"basis\": \"RECEIPT\",\n      \"description\": \"optionalEnvBoolean silently returns false for unrecognized environment values, masking misconfiguration.\",\n      \"citations\":